WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.460
Most problems have several conditions, and they are

00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:04.710
not equally powerful.

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:07.500
One of them usually cuts the possibilities down

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:08.170
to a handful.

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:11.630
Start with that one, and the others become quick checks.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:14.920
Starting with a weak condition leaves you searching

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:16.290
through hundreds of cases.

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:19.430
Starting with the strongest can leave three or four.

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:22.700
Choosing where to begin is a strategy decision worth ten

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:23.650
seconds of thought.

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:27.720
A two-digit number is a perfect square, and its digits

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:28.630
add to ten.

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:29.670
What is it?

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:32.330
Pause and decide which clue to use first.

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:38.910
The digit-sum clue allows nine numbers.

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:43.250
The square clue allows only six: sixteen, twenty-five,

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:47.570
thirty-six, forty-nine, sixty-four and eighty-one.

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:49.270
Start with the squares.

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:53.660
Add the digits of each: seven, seven, nine,

00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:55.820
thirteen, ten, nine.

00:00:56.530 --> 00:00:58.800
Only sixty-four has digits adding to ten.

00:00:59.270 --> 00:01:00.280
The answer is sixty-four.

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:03.230
A product is another strong restriction.

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:05.650
A rectangle has whole-number sides,

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:08.190
area twenty-four and perimeter twenty.

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:12.330
The area allows only four shapes: one by twenty-four,

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:16.230
two by twelve, three by eight, and four by six.

00:01:22.972 --> 00:01:23.110
It is four by six.

00:01:23.630 --> 00:01:25.720
Certain features point to certain tools.

00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:27.440
A product suggests factors.

00:01:28.050 --> 00:01:29.640
A fixed total suggests parts.

00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:32.100
A repeating process suggests a cycle.

00:01:32.410 --> 00:01:33.780
An order suggests a line.

00:01:34.450 --> 00:01:36.860
These are suggestions to try, not guarantees.

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:39.000
List the conditions.

00:01:39.910 --> 00:01:42.160
Start with the one that leaves the fewest possibilities.

00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:44.100
Use the rest as checks.

00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:47.990
Notebook challenge: a number between fifty and one

00:01:47.990 --> 00:01:50.900
hundred is a multiple of thirteen and is odd.

00:01:51.490 --> 00:01:52.260
What could it be?
